  "prompt": "Which acquisition channels bring customers who leave? For each acquisition_channel (in accounts), LedgerLoop's logo churn rate for the second half of 2025: of the accounts with MRR at the end of June 2025 (a row in mrr_monthly for June 2025), the share with a churn event (event_type churn in subscription_events) dated from 1 July to 31 December 2025. Count each account once, even if it churned twice; one that churned and came back still counts as churned. An account that started after June 2025 is in neither count. Return four columns, in this order: acquisition_channel, accounts_at_start, churned_accounts and churn_rate, as a share (0.02 for 2%), not rounded. Return one row per channel with a base. Any row order is fine.",
